      ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x) = 5\\log_{3} x\\ln x$, find $f^{′}(x)$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=5\\log_{3} x$ and $v(x)=\\ln x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =(5\\log_{3} x)^{′}\\ln x+5\\log_{3} x(\\ln x)^{′} \\\\  & =(\\frac{5}{x \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}})(\\ln x)+(5\\log_{3} x)(\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\log_{3} x}{x} + \\frac{5\\ln x}{x\\ln 3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
